{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1717","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Madoka and The Best University"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Madoka wants to enter to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Novosibirsk State University"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", but in the entrance exam she came across a very difficult task:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given an integer $$$n$$$, it is required to calculate $$$\\sum{\\operatorname{lcm}(c, \\gcd(a, b))}$$$, for all triples of positive integers $$$(a, b, c)$$$, where $$$a + b + c = n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem $$$\\gcd(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$, and $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Least_common_multiple"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"least common multiple"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solve this problem for Madoka and help her to enter to the best university!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and the only line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print exactly one interger — $$$\\sum{\\operatorname{lcm}(c, \\gcd(a, b))}$$$. Since the answer can be very large, then output it modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n69228\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n778304278\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there is only one suitable triple $$$(1, 1, 1)$$$. So the answer is $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1, \\gcd(1, 1)) = \\operatorname{lcm}(1, 1) = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1, \\gcd(3, 1)) + \\operatorname{lcm}(1, \\gcd(2, 2)) + \\operatorname{lcm}(1, \\gcd(1, 3)) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, \\gcd(2, 1)) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, \\gcd(1, 2)) + \\operatorname{lcm}(3, \\gcd(1, 1)) = \\operatorname{lcm}(1, 1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(1, 2) + \\operatorname{lcm}(1, 1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, 1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, 1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(3, 1) = 1 + 2 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 = 11$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1717E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1717/problem/E"}